data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"With margin $d = r_c - r_r$, the per-pair loss is $-\\log \\sigma(d) = \\operatorname{softplus}(-d)$.\nUse the split form $\\max(x, 0) + \\log(1 + e^{-|x|})$ with $x = -d$ so the exponential never sees a\nlarge positive argument. The accuracy is the mean of the indicator $d > 0$, cast to the input dtype."},"hints_note":null}

